Package: devjam-plasma-defaults
Version: 1.1-1
Section: kde
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: devjam-wallpapers
Recommends: sddm-theme-breeze
Enhances: plasma-desktop
Maintainer: Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>
Description: KDE Plasma defaults by devjam
 System-wide defaults in /etc/xdg for KDE Plasma and its applications.
 KConfig reads these before ~/.config, so every user starts with them and
 can still change each setting:
 .
  - Dolphin: filter bar, full-width status bar, zoom slider, no menu bar,
    preview plugins
  - single click to open, no Delete command next to Move to Trash
  - Konsole uses the profile Default.profile when a user has it (the
    Debian Live image puts it in /etc/skel), KIO confirmations, an
    empty session at login, region and formats (English with Dutch
    formats)
  - lock screen with the CLS wallpaper (devjam-wallpapers)
  - SDDM theme Breeze (/etc/sddm.conf.d/10-devjam-theme.conf)
  - SDDM starts the X server with -keeptty, which systemd-logind
    integration needs (/etc/sddm.conf.d/20-devjam-x11.conf)
